Atlas overlay patch 0100: ui/kit-chrome-hooks
Why: the lead wants Atlas to have its own interface instead of the engine's restyled chrome (ADR 0062).
The Kit chrome (chrome/browser/ui/atlas/kit, new files) draws the toolbar and the tab sidebar as views
of our own with the WolOS Kit numbers and re-hosts the engine's leaf controls that carry engine logic
(omnibox, pinned actions with Downloads, extensions, app menu), so extensions, profiles and prefs stay
the engine's. This patch is only the hook lines: ToolbarView::Init() installs the Kit toolbar,
ToolbarView::Layout(), CalculatePreferredSize() and GetMinimumSize() defer to it when it is there, and
the BrowserView constructor puts the Kit sidebar into the vertical tab strip region. Everything is off
unless the browser starts with --atlas-kit-chrome (phase 1 of ADR 0062: the patch-based chrome stays
the shipped look until the Kit chrome passes the reel check).
Files: chrome/browser/ui/views/toolbar/toolbar_view.cc, chrome/browser/ui/views/toolbar/BUILD.gn,
chrome/browser/ui/views/frame/browser_view.cc
Test filter: *AtlasKit*
Rebase risk: M (toolbar_view.cc and browser_view.cc are hot files; the hunks are one include, one call
in Init, one early return in Layout, two early returns in the size methods, one call after the vertical
region is made)
Release: 0.13
License: GPL-3.0-or-later (hunks in files the inherited series patches)
Verified at: 156.0.8078.79, prepared tree with the inherited and platform series applied

